+## Remote development preview
+
+Set `IMPECCABLE_LIVE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` to the browser-facing helper URL before
+starting Live, for example `https://preview.example/__gestalt_live/`. Use the
+same setting for helper and injection commands. HTTP(S) origins and path prefixes
+are supported; trailing slashes are normalized. Userinfo, queries and fragments
+are rejected. Stop the helper before changing this setting. Without it, existing
+`http://localhost:PORT` behavior is unchanged.
+
+The helper still binds to `127.0.0.1`. Your development reverse proxy must forward
+that prefix to the helper, strip the prefix, and support streaming SSE. Protect
+all proxy routes with your preview authentication; the helper's token checks
+remain in place. Use the actual app preview URL to open the page, not the helper
+prefix. With the setting active, `live-generate --open --dev-url <preview-url>`
+reports the page URL for the remote browser instead of invoking a server-side
+browser opener. The boot JSON also reports `publicBaseUrl`. Existing CSP meta
+patches use the configured helper origin; any CSP response headers must allow
+that origin for development scripts and connections. This does not authorize
+changes to production CSP, and requires no Playwright runtime dependency.
